# jigsawOS and jigWear -- Developer Documentation

  This is some documentation that is useful for those who wish to make applets and extensions for jigsawOS and its wearable mode, jigWear.
  This will be updated at some point, as I don't know what I'm actually doing.

  
  # -- jigsawOS Guidelines

  - Make sure your applet is easy to use. (ask people for feedback if unsure)
  - The code for your applet should be optimised, as the micro:bit has a very limited amount of memory.
    - Ask people for testing and feedback if unsure.
  - There are two versions of the BBC micro:bit. Please specify and make a different version of the applet if it needs v2 features. (eg. speaker, microphone)

    
  # -- jigWear Guidelines

  - jigWear applets will be used on the go, and while on the move. Make sure they are easy to navigate, and not distracting or complicated.
  - They should take advantage of certain parts of the micro:bit v1 and v2 hardware, such as the accelerometer, etc.
